A||||2||Ken Wittlief||Motivation to finish restoring my car - cruise nite at Fairport||||1||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||06-27-2001||09:41 AM||||I havent done much work on my '85SE in the last couple weeks, I got two wheels cleaned up, still need to paint the hood, the car is running great and Im having too much fun driving it.<P> Last night I went to Cruise Nite in Fairport, NY - just north of the canal a parking lot is roped off and people bring their old/sports/show cars for display - hang around the canal park - have dinner or ice cream - listen to a band<P>  I walked around and looked at all the various cars - no Fieros! A couple of guys had there everyday driver vettes there - nothing special about them - with the front hoods open, like "hey look at this" - like nobody has ever seen a recent model vette before.<P>  If my front hood wasnt half sanded down with primer showing I would have been tempted to pull it in.<P>  Now I have to get the paint and wheels finished so I can pull it in, park it next to a vette, and put a sign on it:<P>   Pontiac Fiero: The only TRUE two passenger MID ENGINE production SPORTS CAR EVER made in the USA!<P> BTW: if any local owners want to hold up the Fiero end of the weekly gathering - its every tuesday nite @ 7PM, just off main street, north of the lift bridge, behind the Box Factory resturant.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-27-2001||06:34 PM||||Had I known about the Fairport drive in, I'd been over.  I went to one in Greece.  The parking lot was overstuffed with cars and no place for a wee Fiero to park.  I did see a nice 65 Pontiac Catalina that had been special ordered with bucket seats and 4 on the floor.  A 2+2 option in the base Catalina.  389 w 4bbl. I'll have to check out the Fairport drive in on 7/10.  I should have both my Fieros home by then.<P>There will be a car show at Pinaways Park in Spencerport 7/28, and a POCI all Pontiac show at Pieler Pontiac 8/26.  Usually we will get 5 or 6 Fieros to that show.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||06-28-2001||09:17 AM||||hey maybe I'll run into you at one of those. If not I'll back up and try again (c:<P>there people use to bring there show cars to one of the hotdog stands up by Seabreeze - right up on the lake by the bay, one night a week last year.<P>I dont remember which day, and I dont know if they still do it this year.<P>I will also stop at the fairport Cruise nite next tues and find out how long they are gonna keep having them.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-28-2001).]||||reg||1
